### TLDR; Quick Answer

**Can I automate my LinkedIn content creation using Claude AI?** Yes.

You can put your LinkedIn strategy on autopilot using the Claude Desktop app in **Cowork mode**. First, create a project base and feed Claude your past top-performing posts to train its semantic understanding of your tone. Then, use a master prompt to generate a custom drafting skill and a 30-day content calendar. Finally, set a scheduled task for Claude to automatically draft your daily post using that custom skill every morning. You just review it over coffee and hit post!

## The Ultimate Guide to Automating Your LinkedIn with Claude AI

We are in an era where the world is fast moving and manual social media management can be a bottleneck.

Most creators and founders think they can grow a personal brand on LinkedIn by posting once in a while because it requires dedicating two hours a day to writing. But with the rapid evolution of Generative AI and Large Language Models (LLMs), you can now build a automated, highly personalized LinkedIn workflow using off-the-shelf features inside **Claude**.

You do not need to be a developer. You do not need to know Python. By leveraging Claude Desktop and custom skills, you can train an AI agent to write exactly like you, optimizing for the exact B2B pain points your audience searches for.

Here is the exact, six-step, no-code framework to put your content strategy on autopilot.

### Step 1: Prepare Your Browser Environment

To allow Claude to access live context and function as a true AI agent, we need to connect the environment.

- Make sure you have the [**Claude browser extension**](https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/claude/fcoeoabgfenejglbffodgkkbkcdhcgfn) set up and enabled.
- Ensure you are logged into **LinkedIn** on the exact same browser so Claude has the appropriate session access.

### Step 2: Establish "My LinkedIn Base" in Cowork Mode

You need to create an isolated, dedicated environment for your content engine so the AI retains your specific context over time.

- Open the [**Claude Desktop**](https://claude.com/download) app.
- Make sure you switch your environment into **Cowork mode**.
- Create a new project workspace that we will work out of.
- Give it the name: **"My LinkedIn Ops Base"** and a description: ***"Help me learn from the internet and build a LinkedIn content strategy with automated planning and content drafting."***

### Step 3: Train the AI and Generate the 30-Day Plan

An AI ghostwriter is only useful if it actually sounds like you. Nobody wants to post generic AI slop. We need to train Claude using your historical data, identify high-performing hooks & angles, and generate our strategy.

Open a new chat within your workspace and paste in the master prompt below:

```
Using browser tool analyze my top posts over the past year from my LinkedIn creator analytics. Then expand each post to learn how I write, what formats perform best, what topics, hooks and angles were winners. Adapt these learnings to <my niche> and <sub-niche> and enhance them with the up to date research on what works best on LinkedIn in this niche and sub-niche. Then use these learnings to build a repeatable skill. Finally, research to find most common questions people ask for said niche on Linkedin, reddit, etc and create another doc with a 30 day plan along with the idea, format of post, format and idea attached media (image or carousel) and a prompt to invoke along with the skill we create to draft each days post.

```

Once Claude finishes analyzing your tone, generating your strategy, and building a custom drafting skill, click "Save Skill".

### Step 4: Schedule the Daily Automation Task

Now, we put the machine to work so you don't have to trigger it manually every day.

- Inside Cowork mode, set up a **scheduled task**.
- Instruct the task to read your newly generated 30-day plan and invoke the custom skill you just created. Program it to draft that specific day's post every single day in the morning.

```
Read my 30 day posting plan and draft the post for the day using the <your skill name here> with Wednesday 24 June, 2026 as Day 1.
```

### Step 5: Review Over Coffee and Post

Your generative AI content machine is now live. Every morning, Claude executes the scheduled task, reads the calendar, applies your unique tone of voice via the custom skill, and drafts an algorithm-optimized post.

- Finally, review the draft over your morning coffee, make any necessary human tweaks, and just post!

You maintain 100% control over your personal brand, but you have successfully eliminated the friction of the blinking cursor.
